# HF (hydrogen fluoride) / 6-31G -- the validation fixture for the three
# convergence tests, replacing C2/STO-3G.
#
# 11 orbitals, 5 alpha / 5 beta, ndet = 213444.
#
# WHY NOT C2/STO-3G: its ground state is DOUBLY DEGENERATE (FCI roots 0 and 1
# both -74.6406501646, partners 0x3f/0x6f and 0x6f/0x3f at +/-1.000000). Any
# mixture of degenerate eigenstates is itself an eigenstate at the same energy,
# so the imaginary-time dynamics apply no restoring force within the manifold
# and the walker population random-walks between the partners. Measured, varying
# only the equilibration length:
#
#   equil    partner/anchor    E_proj          sigma vs exact
#   20000    -0.861            -74.6172886     +2.62
#   40000    -1.674            -74.6413697     -0.06
#   60000    -3.833            -74.7503958     -5.57
#
# The projected energy is therefore not measuring what it claims to on C2, and
# LONGER equilibration makes it worse -- the opposite of the usual intuition.
# A fixture whose estimator degrades with more sampling cannot validate
# "production-length convergence" (test 1) or "walker-population convergence"
# (test 2). The re-anchoring in the driver mitigates it but the fixture is still
# the wrong instrument for the question.
#
# WHY HF/6-31G:
#   - closed-shell singlet, strongly bound, NON-degenerate ground state
#     (verified: roots 0 and 1 separated by a large gap, see below)
#   - ndet = 213444, which is 14.8x N2/STO-3G and 4.8x C2 -- the population
#     sweep spans 0.047-0.469 walkers/determinant, entirely below saturation
#     (C2 saturated at 44100 walkers; HF does not until 213444)
#   - FCI reference still affordable (~9 min), so all three tests keep the
#     deterministic comparison they are defined against
#   - heteronuclear, so no inversion symmetry to create accidental degeneracies
#
# MEASURED (2026-09-02), which is why this fixture is trusted rather than assumed:
#
#   RHF            -99.9834089314
#   FCI root 0    -100.1156979102   <- the reference for all three tests
#   FCI root 1     -99.7369526906
#   gap             0.378745 Eh = 10.31 eV   -> NON-DEGENERATE
#
# Compare C2/STO-3G, whose roots 0 and 1 are separated by 0.00e+00 Eh. The
# non-degeneracy was VERIFIED with nroots 2 rather than argued from chemical
# intuition -- that is exactly the check C2 failed, and asserting it from the
# closed-shell singlet label would have repeated the mistake.
#
# ndet = 213444; FCI reference cost ~9 min at 2 threads.
#
# Geometry: experimental r(H-F) = 0.917 Angstrom.

%begin_control
    basis       6-31g
    calculation energy
    verbosity   verbose
    basis_type  cartesian
%end_control

%begin_scf
    scf_type    rhf
    correlation fciqmc
    ci_max_dim  400000

    fciqmc_walkers         50000
    fciqmc_timestep        0.001
    fciqmc_shift_damping   0.3
    fciqmc_shift_restoring 0.05
    fciqmc_shift_interval  5
    fciqmc_granularity     1.0
    fciqmc_initiator       0.0
    fciqmc_equilibration   20000
    fciqmc_steps           10000
    fciqmc_spawn_attempts  1
    fciqmc_seed            20250901

    use_diis    .true.
    diis_dim    8
    save_checkpoint .false.
    engine      os
    guess       hcore
%end_scf

%begin_geom
    coord_type  cartesian
    coord_units angstrom
    use_symm    .false.
%end_geom

%begin_coords
2
0   1
F     0.000000     0.000000     0.000000
H     0.000000     0.000000     0.917000
%end_coords
